
Written:
  /srv/mnema/.env   (secrets inside, mode 600)
  /srv/mnema/docker-compose.yml

Owner account for the first sign-in:
  user      admin
  password  example-password
  (also in .env as ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD)

What to do next:
  1. Start it, in the folder with the two files:
       docker compose up -d --wait
  2. Open http://localhost:8080 in your browser.
  3. Sign in as "admin" with the password above.
  4. Change the password (your profile settings, Password), then delete the ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD line from .env.
  5. Try voice: open the page in a second browser tab, sign in with a second account (Admin > Invites) and join the same voice channel. Only this computer can open this address; to invite others later, set PUBLIC_URL=https://chat.example.com in .env (doc/operations.md).

Update later: docker compose pull && docker compose up -d
